HST Office: HST Sheets results and files follow the leading spreadsheet application (owner 18/11: in 1.0.3).

- Booleans in text context: "a"&TRUE is "aTRUE" (was "a1"), and CONCATENATE, CONCAT, TEXTJOIN, LEFT, LEN,
  UPPER, SUBSTITUTE, EXACT and TEXT see TRUE/FALSE as the text "TRUE"/"FALSE" (LEN(TRUE) 4, LEFT(TRUE,2) "TR",
  EXACT(TRUE,"TRUE") TRUE). Any boolean result counts: TRUE/FALSE, comparisons, AND, ISNUMBER... Numbers and
  arithmetic are unchanged. Scope: documents with the leading application's formula syntax (the HST Sheets
  default), .xlsx/.xls files, and .ods saved by HST Sheets from now on; an .ods without the HST mark
  (LibreOffice, HST Sheets 1.0.2 and older) keeps its numbers, also when recalculated and saved again.
  Logic in sc/source/core/hst/hstlogicaltext.cxx; hooks: ScInterpreter::GetString and ScText, the document's
  mode (ScDocument member), set by the .xlsx/.xls import.
- .ods marks in an HST namespace (urn:hst-office:names:calc:xmlns:hstcalc:1.0, prefix hstcalc), ignored by
  other ODF consumers: office:spreadsheet hstcalc:logical-text="text", and hstcalc:dynamic-array="true" on the
  anchor of a dynamic array, so a spilling formula reopens as a dynamic array (before, an .ods round trip
  turned it into a fixed Ctrl+Shift+Enter array). Logic in sc/source/filter/xml/hstodsextension.cxx; hooks in
  the .ods export (namespace, office:spreadsheet, matrix anchor) and import (office:spreadsheet, cell,
  matrix range).
- MROUND of a number and a multiple of different signs is #NUM! (MROUND(5,-2) was 6), the vendor's documented
  result; also in the OpenCL kernel. The upstream function test file expects the error.

Test: CppunitTest_sc_hst_excel_parity (booleans in a new document, after .xlsx and .ods round trips, an older
.ods keeps numbers, the HST mark; MROUND examples), CppunitTest_sc_hst_dynamic_array_acceptance
(testOdsKeepsDynamicArrays), CppunitTest_sc_mathematical_functions_test (mround.fods).

More results of the leading spreadsheet application (owner 18/11 21:15), same scope as the booleans:
- #CALC!, a new error value (FormulaError::Calculation, no opcode: the compiler reads and writes the constant
  "#CALC!"): an empty FILTER without if_empty, SEQUENCE with 0 rows or columns, GROUPBY/PIVOTBY without rows
  (before #VALUE!). ERROR.TYPE gives 14 for it and 9 for #SPILL! (before #N/A). Status bar text with a
  Vietnamese translation. .xlsx has no #CALC! cell value: the cached value is #VALUE! (as for #SPILL!) and
  recalculation gives #CALC! again; .ods keeps the error and the constant. In an .ods without the HST mark the
  old errors stay.
- FILTERXML returns a node whose text is a plain decimal number as a number (ISNUMBER(FILTERXML("<a><b>1</b>
  </a>","//b")) is TRUE).
- SUM, AVERAGE, PRODUCT and SUMSQ count a number typed as text directly as an argument (SUM("1",2) is 3);
  text in cells and ranges is still ignored, other text is still #VALUE!.
- ISOMITTED is a boolean, also through LAMBDA and LET (=LAMBDA(a,b,ISOMITTED(b))(1,) shows TRUE, before 1):
  the result of a LAMBDA call keeps the number format type of its body.
Logic in sc/source/core/hst/hstexcelfunctions.cxx; hooks in the interpreter functions, the error tables
(errorcodes.hxx, FormulaCompiler, ScGlobal, XclTools) and globstr.hrc.
Test: CppunitTest_sc_hst_excel_parity (testCalcError, testFilterXmlNumbers, testTextNumberArguments,
testIsOmittedIsLogical; testOlderOdsKeepsNumbers also for SUM).
